{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\drawing\\046.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Step 3", "conf": 0.738, "box": [[853, 119], [989, 130], [984, 188], [849, 177]]}, {"text": "Cut four pieces of the mounting/paper", "conf": 0.906, "box": [[851, 246], [1564, 299], [1560, 351], [847, 298]]}, {"text": "tape a bit longer than each side of the", "conf": 0.915, "box": [[849, 308], [1560, 356], [1557, 406], [846, 358]]}, {"text": "paper. Now apply a little water to the", "conf": 0.895, "box": [[849, 369], [1556, 413], [1553, 462], [846, 418]]}, {"text": "gummed side of the paper using sponge or", "conf": 0.899, "box": [[848, 426], [1552, 473], [1549, 518], [845, 471]]}, {"text": "yourfingers.", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[849, 485], [1058, 498], [1056, 543], [846, 530]]}, {"text": "Step 4", "conf": 0.778, "box": [[147, 626], [304, 626], [304, 682], [147, 682]]}, {"text": "Stick the tape to the sides of. the paper", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[144, 749], [912, 793], [909, 849], [141, 805]]}, {"text": "such that half of it is on the paper and", "conf": 0.932, "box": [[143, 810], [914, 847], [911, 906], [140, 869]]}, {"text": "half on the drawing board.", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[146, 880], [650, 898], [648, 945], [144, 927]]}, {"text": "Stretching is completed. Put the board flat not", "conf": 0.899, "box": [[767, 1266], [1523, 1249], [1524, 1292], [767, 1309]]}, {"text": "awaz", "conf": 0.722, "box": [[590, 1311], [722, 1227], [747, 1266], [614, 1350]]}, {"text": "tilted. Do not put it under a fan. Wait until it", "conf": 0.904, "box": [[767, 1320], [1520, 1302], [1521, 1344], [768, 1362]]}, {"text": "dries. Now it is ready for painting. If you want", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[767, 1376], [1518, 1356], [1519, 1399], [769, 1418]]}, {"text": "to work wet-in-wet, you can start painting", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[764, 1432], [1515, 1411], [1516, 1451], [766, 1472]]}, {"text": "before it dries. In this case you must have your", "conf": 0.904, "box": [[764, 1488], [1513, 1462], [1514, 1502], [766, 1528]]}, {"text": "drawing done because drawing on a wet paper", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[762, 1540], [1514, 1511], [1516, 1558], [764, 1587]]}, {"text": "is difficult. You can not use an eraser on wet", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[759, 1601], [1513, 1565], [1515, 1605], [761, 1641]]}, {"text": "paper.", "conf": 0.811, "box": [[754, 1668], [869, 1656], [873, 1695], [758, 1707]]}, {"text": "Some Basic Watercolour Techniques", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[137, 1943], [915, 1875], [920, 1928], [142, 1996]]}, {"text": "Watercolour is perhaps the most versatile medium. It gives you a wide range of", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[134, 2064], [1503, 1925], [1509, 1983], [140, 2122]]}, {"text": "effects.", "conf": 0.871, "box": [[141, 2124], [284, 2118], [286, 2160], [143, 2166]]}, {"text": "46", "conf": 0.667, "box": [[787, 2222], [848, 2222], [848, 2270], [787, 2270]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[1153, 2231], [1517, 2192], [1522, 2235], [1158, 2274]]}, {"text": "ScannedwithCamScanner", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[1095, 2326], [1274, 2326], [1274, 2343], [1095, 2343]]}]}